WEBVTT

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:10.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday, 29 April. Can you all hear me? Right, let's get going.</v>

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:18.170
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, loud and clear. Anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, what was that second half?</v>

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:22.769
<v Jamie Brennan>I switched it off. Had enough disappointment for one evening.</v>

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:31.809
<v Fiona Doyle>And now the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Can't even recover properly. Just having a moan, before that goes on the job list.</v>

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>The instant stuff's still there. Technically coffee.</v>

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.600
<v Jamie Brennan>After that traffic on the ring road, I'd drink anything. Twenty minutes barely moving.</v>

00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:44.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we become a breakfast radio show—process update?</v>

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.520
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, tested the turbine one gas valve yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished.</v>

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.810
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. That's the one we'd been waiting to hear about.</v>

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:03.219
<v Aisha Begum>Yep. And I signed off the inspection on the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller on Tuesday. Also done, not carrying that forward.</v>

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:05.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, both closed then.</v>

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:14.040
<v Aisha Begum>One observation: saw the pressure on the GT2 dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.140
<v Priya Raman>Right, so a transient, rather than something still sitting low?</v>

00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:24.069
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Just mentioning what I saw, not raising another job today.</v>

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:32.000
<v Sarah Okafor>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the IM2. That's still blocked, just a status update.</v>

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:37.939
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no confirmed delivery date. Nothing firmer than that, unfortunately.</v>

00:01:40.209 --> 00:01:47.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, can you investigate the pressure drop on the water booster today? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:56.349
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the water booster today. First thing ahead of my other bits.</v>

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:02.790
<v Aisha Begum>And that's separate from my GT2 observation, just so we don't muddle the two.</v>

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:08.629
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, understood. The water booster is the production hold-up; that's my first job.</v>

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, thanks.</v>

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.580
<v Fiona Doyle>While I'm on, I'll write up the near miss at the main conveyor by Thursday.</v>

00:02:20.949 --> 00:02:24.800
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, talked over you there—the written account of the near miss?</v>

00:02:25.219 --> 00:02:28.370
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, the write-up. I'll have that done by Thursday.</v>

00:02:29.479 --> 00:02:34.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Fiona Doyle against that one, then. Keeping it separate from the pressure drop.</v>

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.599
<v Fiona Doyle>That's me, yes. Both mine, water booster first.</v>

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you sort the training records for the new starters, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.580
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters.</v>

00:02:53.699 --> 00:02:57.550
<v Fiona Doyle>That's not something you're needing ahead of everything else, is it?</v>

00:02:59.219 --> 00:03:03.770
<v Sarah Okafor>No, whenever you get a chance. There's no fixed deadline on that one.</v>

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.360
<v Hannah Price>Fine, understood. I'll fit that round the other work.</v>

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:15.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, on Friday can you book a contractor to look at the Stretch Wrapper? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:16.479 --> 00:03:22.080
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep—just checking, booking it on Friday, not promising the contractor will actually be here on Friday?</v>

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:28.770
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. The booking on Friday. We're not setting their visit date here.</v>

00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:37.599
<v Jamie Brennan>Okay, I'll book a contractor to look at the Stretch Wrapper on Friday. Important, but not an urgent call-out.</v>

00:03:37.909 --> 00:03:43.509
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good distinction. Booking a bloke and having a bloke stood next to it, very different things.</v>

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:46.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. What else have we got?</v>

00:03:46.409 --> 00:03:51.310
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll take vibration readings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:03:52.449 --> 00:03:54.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. Those readings—top priority please.</v>

00:03:56.849 --> 00:04:00.349
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, top priority. I'll take the readings tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.960
<v Priya Raman>Nine-thirty tomorrow, did you say? Teams clipped the end.</v>

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:10.460
<v Jamie Brennan>Tomorrow at 9:30, yeah. Line 3 Screw and Barrel.</v>

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:16.680
<v Aisha Begum>Heard it that time. Your microphone sounds like it's in a biscuit tin.</v>

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:25.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet by the end of the week? It's urgent.</v>

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:34.670
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, before we move on—I can't get to the forklifts until production gives us a window. That's still the access blocker.</v>

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:44.410
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. Yes, I'll take the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet, by the end of the week. I know it's urgent; access is the snag.</v>

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:54.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, the checks stay urgent and due by the end of the week. The access blocker is noted; we haven't got a window to promise here.</v>

00:04:56.639 --> 00:05:03.290
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, agreed. They're my checks. I'm not calling them checked when I haven't been able to get at them.</v>

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:08.279
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Just wanted that limitation clear, not another job added under my name.</v>

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:16.560
<v Hannah Price>And I'll order spare parts for the guard switch on two by end of day. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:24.180
<v Jamie Brennan>Low priority for the spare parts order, yeah? Not saying a guard switch doesn't matter.</v>

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:32.009
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, the spare parts order is low priority. I'll still get it ordered by end of day.</v>

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:40.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Spare parts for the guard switch on two, by end of day, low priority. Got it.</v>

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:43.899
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:54.600
<v Fiona Doyle>Just checking my order of play: water booster today, first because it's holding production up. Near miss at the main conveyor written up by Thursday.</v>

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.329
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. The production hold-up comes first for you.</v>

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:06.980
<v Tomasz Nowak>And mine's urgent Forklift Fleet pre-use checks, by the end of the week, with that access issue still there. Clear.</v>

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:16.470
<v Jamie Brennan>I've got top-priority vibration readings tomorrow at 9:30, and the Stretch Wrapper contractor booking on Friday. Not an urgent call-out.</v>

00:06:18.009 --> 00:06:25.360
<v Hannah Price>Mine's the training records whenever I get a chance, and the low-priority spare parts order by end of day. All clear.</v>

00:06:26.439 --> 00:06:32.040
<v Aisha Begum>Nothing else from me. The two completed bits are completed, and GT2 was just the observation.</v>

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:37.040
<v Priya Raman>Nothing further electrically. Just that forklift access blocker, as said.</v>

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:45.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. IM2 delivery is still unconfirmed as well, not a fresh action out of this meeting. That's the work covered.</v>

00:06:47.189 --> 00:06:50.339
<v Fiona Doyle>Lovely. Off to enjoy a cup of technically coffee.</v>

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:54.399
<v Jamie Brennan>Don't read the ingredients. Ruins the mystery.</v>

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.310
<v Sarah Okafor>On that inspiring note—thanks, everyone. Speak later.</v>
